# The Dockerfile does `COPY src/ /usr/share/nginx/html/` wholesale, so anything
# sitting in src/ becomes a public URL on the next deploy. These are working
# files that must not:
#
#   src/_fontcompare.html  ->  would publish econ.chrislawrence.ca/_fontcompare.html
#
# src/fonts/ is deliberately NOT excluded: the page adopted Oswald as a real
# webfont (@font-face -> /fonts/oswald.woff2), so the asset has to ship with
# the rule that needs it. Its SIL licence travels beside it in the same
# directory, which is a redistribution condition, not decoration.
src/_*

# Browser-automation scratch: screenshots and page snapshots taken while
# checking the rendered page. Working notes, never image content.
.playwright-mcp/

# Not copied by the Dockerfile, but excluded so a stray `COPY .` in future
# cannot pick them up.
.git/
data/
screenshots/
*.md
